--TEST--
every way an `#[Api]` can contradict the code beside it is refused, and all four are `E0771` — `rule:attributes/api-adds-and-cannot-contradict`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:attributes/core-api-and-the-openapi-document
//
// The four contradictions in one program, which is the half of
// `rule:attributes/api-adds-and-cannot-contradict` a Novis case can ask about:
// the emitted document is a build artefact no program's stdout carries, so
// `crates/nvs-cli/tests/openapi.rs` owns that half and this file owns the
// refusals a person writing Novis meets.
//
// Asserted as four together rather than one per file on purpose. Each is a
// *different* comparison against the declaration, and they share one code, so
// a pass that dropped one of the four still looks right on any single line —
// what pins them is that the build reports four and no fewer.

interface OrderFault {}

class Order {
    public uint $id = 0;
}

class Orders {
    // 1. `errors:` naming something no handler can produce. The name resolves,
    //    and an interface is still not a class a `throw` ever answers with.
    #[Core\Route(path: "/orders/{id}", method: Core\Http\Method::Get, name: "Orders::show")]
    #[Core\Access(allow: Core\Audience::Public)]
    #[Core\Api(errors: [{status: 404, type: OrderFault::class}])]
    public function show(uint $id): Order { return new Order(); }

    // 2. `example:` naming a key the return type does not declare.
    #[Core\Route(path: "/orders", method: Core\Http\Method::Get, name: "Orders::index")]
    #[Core\Access(allow: Core\Audience::Public)]
    #[Core\Api(example: {quantity: 3})]
    public function index(): Order { return new Order(); }

    // 3. A `security:` entry that is not a name.
    #[Core\Route(path: "/orders/count", method: Core\Http\Method::Get, name: "Orders::count")]
    #[Core\Access(allow: Core\Audience::Public)]
    #[Core\Api(security: [404])]
    public function count(): uint { return 0; }

    // 4. An `#[Api]` on a method carrying no `#[Route]`, so it describes
    //    nothing.
    #[Core\Api(tags: ["Orders"])]
    public function helper(): uint { return 1; }
}

echo "unreachable", "\n";
--EXPECT--
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0771]: `OrderFault` is not a class a handler could produce
%A
error[E0771]: `Order` declares no `quantity`
%A
error[E0771]: this `security` entry is not a string
%A
error[E0771]: this `#[Api]` annotates no operation
%A
error: aborting due to 4 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
